  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use the graph for questions 1 - 2.</para>
<figure><media alt="graph of (0, 4) and (4, 0)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/aacd061405bc69664246ed8cf981961e9c6f1bb0"/></media></figure><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="3421aa35-b50d-4c5c-a3b1-441817c24a26"><problem><para>
      <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are on the line? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> answers.</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>["\\((0, 4)\\)", "\\((2, 2)\\)", "\\((-2, 6)\\)"]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answers are \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
